  "job_B14.4.3_20251003_114312": {
    "text": "Dryhten w\u00e6s sprecende \u00f0as word to Moyse & \u00feus cw\u00e6\u00f0: Ic eom dryhten \u00f0in God.\nIc \u00f0e utgel\u00e6dde of Egipta londe & of hiora \u00f0eowdome.\nNe lufa \u00f0u o\u00fere fremde godas ofer me.\nNe minne noman ne cig \u00f0u on idelnesse; for\u00f0on \u00fee \u00f0u ne bist unscyldig wi\u00f0 me, gif \u00f0u on idelnesse cigst\nGemyne \u00fe\u00e6t \u00f0u gehalgige \u00feone r\u00e6sted\u00e6g; wyrcea\u00f0 eow VI dagas & on \u00feam siofo\u00f0an resta\u00f0 eow:\nAra \u00f0inum f\u00e6der & \u00feinre medder, \u00f0a \u00fee Dryhten sealde, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00f0u sie \u00fey leng libbende on eor\u00fean.\nNe sleah \u00f0u.\nNe lige \u00f0u dearnenga.\nNe stala \u00f0u.\nNe s\u00e6ge \u00f0u lease gewitnesse.\nNe wilna \u00f0u \u00feines nehstan ierfes mid unryhte.\nNe wyrc \u00f0e gyldne godas o\u00f0\u00f0e sylfrene.\n\u00deis sint \u00f0a domas \u00fee \u00f0u him settan scealt: Gif hwa gebycgge cristenne \u00feeow, VI gear \u00f0eowige he; \u00f0y\nGif he wif self h\u00e6bbe, gange hio ut mid him.\nGif se hlaford him \u00feonne wif sealde, sie hio & hire bearn \u00fe\u00e6s hlafordes.\nGif se \u00feeowa \u00feonne cwe\u00f0e: Nelle ic from minum hlaforde ne from minum wife, ne from minum bearne\n\u00d0eah hwa gebycgge his dohtor on \u00feeowenne, ne sie hio ealles swa \u00f0eowu swa o\u00f0ru mennenu: nage he\nAc gif he hire ne recce, se \u00f0e hie bohte, l\u00e6te hie freo on el\u00f0eodig folc.\nGif he \u00f0onne alefe his suna mid to h\u00e6manne, do hiere gyfta: locige \u00fe\u00e6t hio h\u00e6bbe hr\u00e6gl; & \u00fe\u00e6t weor\u00f0\nGif he hire \u00feara nan ne do, \u00feonne sie hio frioh.\nSe mon se \u00f0e his gewealdes monnan ofslea, swelte se dea\u00f0e.\nSe \u00f0e hine \u00feonne nedes ofsloge o\u00f0\u00f0e unwillum o\u00f0\u00f0e ungewealdes, swelce hine God swa sende on his\nGif hwa \u00f0onne of giernesse & gewealdes ofslea his \u00feone nehstan \u00feurh searwa, aluc \u00f0u hine from\nSe \u00f0e slea his f\u00e6der o\u00f0\u00f0e his modor, se sceal dea\u00f0e sweltan.\nSe \u00f0e frione forstele & he hine bebycgge, & hit onbest\u00e6led sie, \u00fe\u00e6t he hine bereccean ne m\u00e6ge, swelte\nSe \u00f0e werge his f\u00e6der o\u00f0\u00f0e his modor, swelte se dea\u00f0e.\nGif hwa slea his \u00f0one nehstan mid stane o\u00f0\u00f0e mid fyste, & he \u00feeah utgongan m\u00e6ge bi stafe, begite him\nSe \u00f0e slea his agenne \u00feeowne esne o\u00f0\u00f0e his mennen, & he ne sie id\u00e6ges dead, \u00f0eah he libbe twa niht\nGif he \u00f0onne sie id\u00e6ges dead, \u00f0onne sitte sio scyld on him.\nGif hwa on cease eacniende wif gewerde, bete \u00feone \u00e6werdlan, swa him domeras gereccen.\nGif hio dead sie, selle sawle wi\u00f0 sawle.\nGif hwa o\u00f0rum his eage o\u00f0do, selle his agen fore: to\u00f0 fore te\u00f0, honda wi\u00f0 honda, fet fore fet, b\u00e6rning\nGif hwa aslea his \u00f0eowe o\u00f0\u00f0e his \u00f0eowenne \u00fe\u00e6t eage ut & he \u00feonne hie gedo anigge gefreoge hie for\nGif he \u00feonne \u00f0one to\u00f0 ofaslea, do \u00fe\u00e6t ilce.\nGif oxa ofhnite wer o\u00f0\u00f0e wif, \u00fe\u00e6t hie dead sien, sie he mid stanum ofworpod, & ne sie his fl\u00e6sc eten;\nGif se oxa hnitol w\u00e6re twam dagum \u00e6r o\u00f0\u00f0e \u00f0rim, & se hlaford hit wisse & hine inne betynan nolde, &\nSunu o\u00f0\u00f0e dohtor gif he ofstinge, \u00f0\u00e6s ilcan domes sie he wyr\u00f0e.\nGif he \u00f0onne \u00f0eow o\u00f0\u00f0e \u00f0eowmennen ofstinge, geselle \u00feam hlaforde XXX scillinga seolfres, & se oxa\nGif hwa adelfe w\u00e6terpyt o\u00f0\u00f0e betynedne ontyne & hine eft ne betyne, gelde swelc neat swelc \u00f0\u00e6r on\nGif oxa o\u00f0res monnes oxan gewundige, & he \u00f0onne dead sie, bebycggen \u00feone oxan & h\u00e6bben him \u00fe\u00e6t\nGif se hlaford \u00feonne wisse, \u00fe\u00e6t se oxa hnitol w\u00e6re, & hine healdan nolde, selle him o\u00f0erne oxan fore\nGif hwa forstele o\u00f0res oxan & hine ofslea o\u00f0\u00f0e bebycgge, selle twegen wi\u00f0 & feower sceap wi\u00f0 anum.\nGif he n\u00e6bbe hw\u00e6t he selle, sie he self beboht wi\u00f0 \u00f0am fio.\nGif \u00f0eof brece mannes hus nihtes & he weor\u00f0e \u00fe\u00e6r ofslegen, ne sie he na mansleges scyldig.\nGif he si\u00f0\u00f0an \u00e6fter sunnan upgonge \u00feis de\u00f0, he bi\u00f0 mansleges scyldig & he \u00f0onne self swelte, buton he\nGif mid him cwicum sie funden \u00fe\u00e6t he \u00e6r st\u00e6l, be twyfealdum forgielde hit.\nGif hwa gewerde o\u00f0res monnes wingeard o\u00f0\u00f0e his \u00e6cras o\u00f0\u00f0e his landes awuht, gebete swa hit mon\nGif fyr sie ontended ryt to b\u00e6rnanne, gebete \u00feone \u00e6fwerdelsan se \u00f0\u00e6t fyr ontent.\nGif hwa o\u00f0f\u00e6ste his friend fioh, gif he hit self st\u00e6le, forgylde be twyfealdum.\nGif he nyte, hwa hit st\u00e6le, geladige hine selfne, \u00fe\u00e6t he \u00f0\u00e6r nan facn ne gefremede.\nGif hit \u00f0onne cucu feoh w\u00e6re, & he secgge, \u00fe\u00e6t hit here name o\u00f0\u00f0e hit self acw\u00e6le, & gewitnesse\nGif he \u00f0onne gewitnesse n\u00e6bbe, & he him ne getriewe, swerige he \u00feonne.\nGif hwa f\u00e6mnan beswice unbeweddode & hire midsl\u00e6po, forgielde hie & h\u00e6bbe hi si\u00f0\u00f0an him to wife.\nGif \u00f0\u00e6re f\u00e6mnan f\u00e6der hie \u00f0onne sellan nelle, agife he \u00f0\u00e6t feoh \u00e6fter \u00feam weotuman.\n\u00d0a f\u00e6mnan \u00fee gewunia\u00f0 onfon gealdorcr\u00e6ftigan & scinl\u00e6can & wiccan, ne l\u00e6t \u00feu \u00f0a libban.\n& se \u00f0e h\u00e6me mid netene, swelte he dea\u00f0e.\n& se \u00f0e godgeldum onsecge ofer God anne, swelte se dea\u00f0e.\nUtan cumene & el\u00f0eodige ne geswenc \u00f0u no, for\u00f0on \u00f0e ge w\u00e6ron giu el\u00f0eodige on Egipta londe.\n\u00dea wuduwan & \u00fea stiopcild ne sce\u00f0\u00f0a\u00f0 ge, ne hie nawer deria\u00f0.\nGif ge \u00feonne elles do\u00f0, hie cleopia\u00f0 to me, & ic gehiere hie & ic eow \u00feonne slea mid minum sweorde\nGif \u00f0u fioh to borge selle \u00feinum geferan, \u00fee mid \u00fee eardian wille, ne niede \u00f0u hine swa swa niedling &\nGif mon n\u00e6bbe buton anfeald hr\u00e6gl hine mid to wreonne & to werianne, & he hit to wedde selle, \u00e6r\nGif \u00f0u swa ne dest, \u00feonne cleopa\u00f0 he to me, & ic hine gehiere, for\u00f0on \u00f0e ic eom swi\u00f0e mildheort.\nNe t\u00e6l \u00f0u \u00f0inne Dryhten, ne \u00f0one hlaford \u00fe\u00e6s folces ne werge \u00feu.\n\u00deine teo\u00f0an sceattas & \u00feine frumripan gongendes & weaxendes agif \u00feu Gode.\nEal \u00f0\u00e6t fl\u00e6sc \u00fe\u00e6t wildeor l\u00e6fen ne eten ge \u00fe\u00e6t, ac sella\u00f0 hit hundum.\nLeases monnes word ne rec \u00f0u no \u00fe\u00e6s to gehieranne, ne his domas ne ge\u00f0afa \u00f0u, ne nane gewitnesse\nNe wend \u00f0u \u00f0e no on \u00fe\u00e6s folces unr\u00e6d & unryht gewill on hiora spr\u00e6ce & geclysp ofer \u00f0in ryht, & \u00f0\u00e6s\nGif \u00f0e becume o\u00f0res mannes giemeleas fioh on hond \u00feeah hit sie \u00f0in feond, gecy\u00f0e hit him.\nDem \u00f0u swi\u00f0e emne.\nNe dem \u00f0u o\u00f0erne dom \u00feam welegan, o\u00f0erne \u00f0am earman; ne o\u00f0erne \u00feam liofran & o\u00f0erne \u00feam la\u00f0ran\nOnscuna \u00f0u a leasunga.\nSo\u00f0f\u00e6stne man & unscyldigne ne acwele \u00f0u \u00feone n\u00e6fre.\nNe onfoh \u00f0u n\u00e6fre medsceattum, for\u00f0on hie ablenda\u00f0 ful oft wisra monna ge\u00f0oht & hiora word\n\u00deam el\u00f0eodegan & utan cumenan ne l\u00e6t \u00f0u no uncu\u00f0lice wi\u00f0 hine, ne mid nanum unryhtum \u00feu hine ne\nNe swergen ge n\u00e6fre under h\u00e6\u00f0ne godas, ne on nanum \u00f0ingum ne cleopien ge to him.\n\u00deis sindan \u00f0a domas \u00fee se \u00e6lmihtega God self sprecende w\u00e6s to Moyse & him bebead to healdanne.\n& si\u00f0\u00f0an se ancenneda Dryhtnes sunu, ure God, \u00fe\u00e6t is h\u00e6lend Crist, on middangeard cwom, he cw\u00e6\u00f0,\n\u00d0a \u00e6fter his \u00f0rowunge, \u00e6r \u00feam \u00fee his apostolas tofarene w\u00e6ron geond ealle eor\u00f0an to l\u00e6ranne, & \u00fea\n\u00dea hie ealle \u00e6tsomne w\u00e6ron, hie sendan \u00e6rendwrecan to Antiohhia & to Syrie, Cristes \u00e6 to l\u00e6ranne.\n\u00dea hie \u00f0a ongeaton, \u00fe\u00e6t him ne speow, \u00f0a sendon hie \u00e6rendgewrit to him.\n\u00deis is \u00f0onne \u00fe\u00e6t \u00e6rendgewrit \u00fee \u00f0a apostolas sendon ealle to Antiohhia & to Syria & to cilicia, \u00f0a\n\u00d0a apostolas & \u00fea eldran bro\u00f0or h\u00e6lo eow wysca\u00f0; & we eow cy\u00f0a\u00f0, \u00fe\u00e6t we geascodon, \u00fe\u00e6t ure\n\u00d0a gesomnodon we us ymb \u00f0\u00e6t, & us eallum gelicode \u00f0a, \u00fe\u00e6t we sendon Paulus & Barnaban; \u00f0a\nMid him we sendon Iudam & Silam, \u00fe\u00e6t eow \u00fe\u00e6t ilce seccgen.\n\u00de\u00e6m halgan Gaste w\u00e6s ge\u00f0uht & us, \u00fe\u00e6t we nane byr\u00f0enne on eow settan noldon ofer \u00fe\u00e6t \u00f0e eow\nOf \u00f0issum anum dome mon m\u00e6g ge\u00f0encean, \u00fe\u00e6t he \u00e6ghwelcne on ryht gedeme\u00f0; ne \u00f0earf he nanra\nGe\u00f0ence he, \u00fe\u00e6t he nanum men ne deme \u00fe\u00e6t he nolde \u00f0\u00e6t he him demde, gif he \u00f0one dom ofer hine\nSi\u00f0\u00f0an \u00f0\u00e6t \u00fea gelamp, \u00fe\u00e6t monega \u00f0eoda Cristes geleafan onfengon, \u00fea wurdon monega seono\u00f0as\nHie \u00f0a gesetton, for \u00f0\u00e6re mildheortnesse \u00fee Crist l\u00e6rde, \u00e6t m\u00e6stra hwelcre misd\u00e6de \u00fe\u00e6tte \u00f0a\nButon \u00e6t hlafordsearwe hie nane mildheortnesse ne dorston gecwe\u00f0an, for\u00feam \u00f0e God \u00e6lmihtig \u00feam\nHie \u00f0a on monegum seno\u00f0um monegra menniscra misd\u00e6da bote gesetton, & on monega seno\u00f0bec hie\nIc \u00f0a \u00e6lfred cyning \u00feas tog\u00e6dere gegaderode & awritan het, monege \u00feara \u00fee ure foregengan heoldon,\nFor\u00f0am ic ne dorste ge\u00f0ristl\u00e6can \u00feara minra awuht fela on gewrit settan, for\u00f0am me w\u00e6s uncu\u00f0,\nAc \u00f0a \u00f0e ic gemette aw\u00f0er o\u00f0\u00f0e on Ines d\u00e6ge, mines m\u00e6ges, o\u00f0\u00f0e on Offan Mercna cyninges o\u00f0\u00f0e\nIc \u00f0a \u00e6lfred Westseaxna cyning eallum minnum witum, \u00feas geeowde, & hie \u00f0a cw\u00e6don, \u00fe\u00e6t him",
